            "style": "link"
          }
        ]
      },
      "name": "EnvironmentTabs"
    },
    {
      "type": 1,
      "content": {
        "json": "### Organization overview\nThe same investigation surface combines reported Log4j findings, all-posture recommendation evidence, subscription plan evidence, discovered connectors, and Azure/Arc software-inventory gaps. A connected environment with no Log4j findings can still appear in the connector inventory. Counts are not added across scanners, and a visible connector is not proof of a successful scan."
      },
      "conditionalVisibility": {
        "parameterName": "Environment",
        "comparison": "isEqualTo",
        "value": "All"
      },
      "name": "OrganizationGuidance"
    },
    {
      "type": 1,
      "content": {
        "json": "### Azure\nInvestigate native Azure machine, registry/image, Kubernetes, application, and serverless findings together. Use the workload filter to narrow the shared tables. Azure-hosted connector resources do not make AWS/GCP or code findings Azure findings. Organization overview contains Azure subscription plan evidence; it does not automatically establish effective per-resource or external-cloud coverage."
      },
      "conditionalVisibility": {
        "parameterName": "Environment",
        "comparison": "isEqualTo",
        "value": "Azure"
      },
      "name": "AzureGuidance"
    },
    {
      "type": 1,
      "content": {
        "json": "### AWS\nCloud-source, provider, and available Arc cloud metadata identify AWS findings, including AWS machines represented through Azure Arc. Connector offerings/settings, AWS account scope, discovery permissions, and scanning support must be verified separately. Azure anchor subscription pricing is not an AWS entitlement verdict."
      },
      "conditionalVisibility": {
        "parameterName": "Environment",
        "comparison": "isEqualTo",
        "value": "AWS"
      },
      "name": "AWSGuidance"
    },
    {
      "type": 1,
      "content": {
        "json": "### GCP\nCloud-source, provider, and available Arc cloud metadata identify GCP findings, including GCP machines represented through Azure Arc. Check connected project/organization scope, connector offerings, permissions, and supported compute/image scanning. Missing project findings do not establish that the project is covered."
      },
      "conditionalVisibility": {
        "parameterName": "Environment",
        "comparison": "isEqualTo",
        "value": "GCP"
      },
      "name": "GCPGuidance"
    },
    {
      "type": 1,
      "content": {
        "json": "### Hybrid / Arc\nThis view contains other Arc/hybrid findings, not a claim that every resource is on-premises. Recognized AWS/GCP provenance takes precedence over Arc representation. Inventory evidence retains disconnected Arc machines so a connection gap is not hidden; unsupported and never-onboarded assets can still be absent. Cloud agentless disk scanning does not automatically cover on-premises machines."
      },
      "conditionalVisibility": {
        "parameterName": "Environment",
        "comparison": "isEqualTo",
        "value": "Hybrid"
      },
      "name": "HybridGuidance"
    },
    {
      "type": 1,
      "content": {
        "json": "### DevOps - GitHub, Azure DevOps, GitLab, and reported code findings\nDiscover connected code environments even when they have no reported Log4j finding. Agentless code scanning/SBOM is currently **Preview** for supported Azure DevOps/GitHub scenarios; do not assume that GitLab has the same agentless feature support. A connector, IaC scan, secret scan, or Java SAST alone does not establish Java dependency coverage.\n\nFor SBOM inventory, use **Cloud Security Explorer > repository type > Application > Has installed software > Name / Version** with the actual reported Log4j package names. ARG recommendation rows below are not an SBOM. Follow code-to-runtime relationships to the owning repository/build, update dependencies, rebuild, redeploy, and re-scan.\n\n[Code scanning](https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/defender-for-cloud/agentless-code-scanning) | [Queryable SBOM](https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/defender-for-cloud/query-software-bill-of-materials) | [DevOps feature/entitlement matrix](https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/defender-for-cloud/devops-support) | [Code-to-runtime mapping](https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/defender-for-cloud/container-image-mapping)"
      },
      "conditionalVisibility": {
        "parameterName": "Environment",
        "comparison": "isEqualTo",
        "value": "DevOps"
      },
      "name": "DevOpsGuidance"
    },
    {
      "type": 1,
      "content": {
        "json": "### Other / external environments\nThis view retains unclassified findings and external connectors, including reported Docker Hub/JFrog integrations. A new or missing source/provider value is not silently assigned to Azure merely because its connector is stored in an Azure subscription. Inspect raw source, resource type, connector ID, and workload context; use Organization overview to reconcile totals."
      },
      "conditionalVisibility": {
        "parameterName": "Environment",
        "comparison": "isEqualTo",
        "value": "Other"
      },
      "name": "OtherGuidance"
    },
    {
      "type": 3,
      "content": {
        "version": "KqlItem/1.0",
        "query": "securityresources\n| where subscriptionId in~ ({Subscription:subid})\n| where type =~ 'microsoft.security/assessments'\n| extend Resource = coalesce(tostring(properties.resourceDetails.Id), tostring(properties.resourceDetails.id), tostring(properties.resourceDetails.AzureResourceId)), ResourceType = tolower(tostring(properties.resourceDetails.ResourceType)), CloudSource = tostring(properties.resourceDetails.Source), ConnectorId = tostring(properties.resourceDetails.ConnectorId)\n| extend ContextLookupId = tolower(iff(ResourceType startswith 'microsoft.hybridcompute/', Resource, ConnectorId))\n| join kind=leftouter (\n    resources\n    | where subscriptionId in~ ({Subscription:subid})\n    | where type in~ ('microsoft.hybridcompute/machines', 'microsoft.security/securityconnectors')\n    | project ContextLookupId = tolower(id), ArcCloudProvider = tostring(properties.cloudMetadata.provider), ConnectorPlatform = tostring(properties.environmentName)\n) on ContextLookupId\n| extend Environment = case(CloudSource in~ ('AzureDevOps', 'Github', 'GitLab') or ConnectorPlatform in~ ('AzureDevOps', 'Github', 'GitLab') or ResourceType contains 'devops' or ResourceType contains 'github' or ResourceType contains 'gitlab', 'DevOps', CloudSource =~ 'AWS' or ArcCloudProvider =~ 'AWS' or ConnectorPlatform =~ 'AWS' or ResourceType startswith 'microsoft.awsconnector/', 'AWS', CloudSource =~ 'GCP' or ArcCloudProvider =~ 'GCP' or ConnectorPlatform =~ 'GCP' or ResourceType startswith 'microsoft.gcpconnector/', 'GCP', CloudSource in~ ('DockerHub', 'JFrog') or ConnectorPlatform in~ ('DockerHub', 'JFrog'), 'Other', ResourceType startswith 'microsoft.hybridcompute/', 'Hybrid', CloudSource =~ 'Azure' and (isempty(ConnectorId) or ConnectorPlatform =~ 'Azure'), 'Azure', 'Other')\n| extend Workload = case(Environment == 'DevOps', 'DevOps', ResourceType has_any ('sites', 'containerapps', 'containergroups', 'lambdafunctions', 'functions'), 'Serverless', ResourceType =~ 'microsoft.containerregistry/registries' or ResourceType has_any ('containerimage', 'containerimages', 'container', 'containers', 'managedclusters', 'connectedclusters', 'eksclusters', 'kubernetesclusters'), 'Containers', ResourceType has_any ('virtualmachines', 'virtualmachinescalesets', 'machines', 'ec2instances', 'computeinstances'), 'Machines', 'Other')\n| where '{Environment}' == 'All' or Environment == '{Environment}'\n| where '{Workload}' == 'All' or Workload == '{Workload}'\n| where properties.metadata.recommendationCategory in~ ('SoftwareUpdate', 'ServiceUpgrade')\n| where tostring(properties.status.code) == 'Unhealthy'\n| extend Software = tostring(properties.additionalData.SoftwareName), AssessmentId = id\n| extend CvesDetails = parse_json(tostring(properties.additionalData.CvesDetails))\n| mv-expand CveDetail = CvesDetails limit 2000\n| extend CVE = toupper(tostring(CveDetail.CveId))\n| where CVE in~ ('CVE-2021-44228', 'CVE-2021-45046', 'CVE-2021-45105', 'CVE-2021-44832') or ('{FindingScope}' == 'AllLog4j' and Software has_any ('log4j', 'log4j2'))\n| where isnotempty(CVE)\n| summarize Recommendations = dcount(AssessmentId), DistinctCVEs = dcount(CVE) by Environment, Workload\n| order by Recommendations desc",
        "size": 0,
        "title": "Reported Log4j findings by environment and workload",
        "noDataMessage": "No matching Log4j findings returned. Verify the selected environment/workload, scan coverage, permissions, and native Defender results before drawing a conclusion.",
        "showExportToExcel": true,
        "showAnalytics": true,
        "queryType": 1,
        "resourceType": "microsoft.resourcegraph/resources",
        "crossComponentResources": [
          "{Subscription}"
        ],
        "visualization": "table",
        "gridSettings": {
          "filter": true
        }
      },
      "name": "Log4jSummary"
    },
    {
      "type": 3,
      "content": {
        "version": "KqlItem/1.0",
        "query": "securityresources\n| where subscriptionId in~ ({Subscription:subid})\n| where type =~ 'microsoft.security/assessments'\n| extend Resource = coalesce(tostring(properties.resourceDetails.Id), tostring(properties.resourceDetails.id), tostring(properties.resourceDetails.AzureResourceId)), ResourceType = tolower(tostring(properties.resourceDetails.ResourceType)), CloudSource = tostring(properties.resourceDetails.Source), ConnectorId = tostring(properties.resourceDetails.ConnectorId)\n| extend ContextLookupId = tolower(iff(ResourceType startswith 'microsoft.hybridcompute/', Resource, ConnectorId))\n| join kind=leftouter (\n    resources\n    | where subscriptionId in~ ({Subscription:subid})\n    | where type in~ ('microsoft.hybridcompute/machines', 'microsoft.security/securityconnectors')\n    | project ContextLookupId = tolower(id), ArcCloudProvider = tostring(properties.cloudMetadata.provider), ConnectorPlatform = tostring(properties.environmentName)\n) on ContextLookupId\n| extend Environment = case(CloudSource in~ ('AzureDevOps', 'Github', 'GitLab') or ConnectorPlatform in~ ('AzureDevOps', 'Github', 'GitLab') or ResourceType contains 'devops' or ResourceType contains 'github' or ResourceType contains 'gitlab', 'DevOps', CloudSource =~ 'AWS' or ArcCloudProvider =~ 'AWS' or ConnectorPlatform =~ 'AWS' or ResourceType startswith 'microsoft.awsconnector/', 'AWS', CloudSource =~ 'GCP' or ArcCloudProvider =~ 'GCP' or ConnectorPlatform =~ 'GCP' or ResourceType startswith 'microsoft.gcpconnector/', 'GCP', CloudSource in~ ('DockerHub', 'JFrog') or ConnectorPlatform in~ ('DockerHub', 'JFrog'), 'Other', ResourceType startswith 'microsoft.hybridcompute/', 'Hybrid', CloudSource =~ 'Azure' and (isempty(ConnectorId) or ConnectorPlatform =~ 'Azure'), 'Azure', 'Other')\n| extend Workload = case(Environment == 'DevOps', 'DevOps', ResourceType has_any ('sites', 'containerapps', 'containergroups', 'lambdafunctions', 'functions'), 'Serverless', ResourceType =~ 'microsoft.containerregistry/registries' or ResourceType has_any ('containerimage', 'containerimages', 'container', 'containers', 'managedclusters', 'connectedclusters', 'eksclusters', 'kubernetesclusters'), 'Containers', ResourceType has_any ('virtualmachines', 'virtualmachinescalesets', 'machines', 'ec2instances', 'computeinstances'), 'Machines', 'Other')\n| where '{Environment}' == 'All' or Environment == '{Environment}'\n| where '{Workload}' == 'All' or Workload == '{Workload}'\n| where properties.metadata.recommendationCategory in~ ('SoftwareUpdate', 'ServiceUpgrade')\n| where tostring(properties.status.code) == 'Unhealthy'\n| extend ResourceName = tostring(properties.resourceDetails.ResourceName), WorkloadDetails = parse_json(tostring(properties.resourceAdditionalData))\n| extend ImageUri = tostring(WorkloadDetails.ImageUri), Repository = tostring(WorkloadDetails.RepositoryDetails.RepositoryName)\n| extend Software = tostring(properties.additionalData.SoftwareName), ScannersDetails = parse_json(tostring(properties.additionalData.ScannersDetails))\n| extend ScannerEntry = coalesce(ScannersDetails.mdvm, ScannersDetails[tostring(bag_keys(ScannersDetails)[0])])\n| extend DetectedVersionData = parse_json(tostring(properties.additionalData.DetectedSoftwareVersions)), ScannerDetectedVersionData = parse_json(tostring(ScannerEntry.DetectedSoftwareVersions))\n| extend DetectedVersions = coalesce(case(gettype(DetectedVersionData) == 'array', strcat_array(DetectedVersionData, ', '), gettype(DetectedVersionData) == 'string', tostring(DetectedVersionData), isnull(DetectedVersionData), '', tostring(properties.additionalData.DetectedSoftwareVersions)), case(gettype(ScannerDetectedVersionData) == 'array', strcat_array(ScannerDetectedVersionData, ', '), gettype(ScannerDetectedVersionData) == 'string', tostring(ScannerDetectedVersionData), isnull(ScannerDetectedVersionData), '', tostring(ScannerEntry.DetectedSoftwareVersions)))\n| extend ScannerFixedVersion = coalesce(tostring(properties.additionalData.FixedVersion), tostring(ScannerEntry.FixedVersion))\n| extend Recommendation = tostring(properties.displayName), RecommendationSeverity = tostring(properties.metadata.severity), AssessmentId = id\n| extend RiskLevel = tostring(properties.risk.level), RiskFactors = properties.risk.riskFactors, AttackPathReferences = properties.risk.attackPathsReferences\n| extend RiskOrder = case(RiskLevel =~ 'Critical', 0, RiskLevel =~ 'High', 1, RiskLevel =~ 'Medium', 2, RiskLevel =~ 'Low', 3, 4)\n| extend RiskLevel = iff(isempty(RiskLevel), 'Not evaluated / no visible context', RiskLevel)\n| extend CvesDetails = parse_json(tostring(properties.additionalData.CvesDetails))\n| mv-expand CveDetail = CvesDetails limit 2000\n| extend CVE = toupper(tostring(CveDetail.CveId)), FixedVersion = coalesce(tostring(CveDetail.FixedVersion), ScannerFixedVersion)\n| where CVE in~ ('CVE-2021-44228', 'CVE-2021-45046', 'CVE-2021-45105', 'CVE-2021-44832') or ('{FindingScope}' == 'AllLog4j' and Software has_any ('log4j', 'log4j2'))\n| where isnotempty(CVE)\n| join kind=leftouter (\n    securityresources\n    | where type =~ 'microsoft.security/cvedetails'\n    | project CVE = toupper(tostring(properties.cveId)), CVESeverity = tostring(properties.severity), CVEMetadata = properties\n) on CVE\n| extend CVESeverity = iff(isempty(CVESeverity), 'Unknown - CVE detail not visible', CVESeverity)\n| order by RiskOrder asc, CVE asc, Resource asc\n| project Environment, Workload, RiskLevel, CVE, CVESeverity, RecommendationSeverity, ResourceName, Resource, Software, DetectedVersions, FixedVersion, ScannersDetails, ImageUri, Repository, RiskFactors, AttackPathReferences, CloudSource, ArcCloudProvider, ConnectorPlatform, ResourceType, ConnectorId, Recommendation, WorkloadDetails, CVEMetadata, AssessmentId, Subscription = subscriptionId",
        "size": 0,
        "title": "Unified Log4j findings - all available reported sources",
        "noDataMessage": "No matching findings returned. Check environment/workload selection, scope, permissions, connector/scanner coverage, and freshness. No rows do not prove safety or absence of attack paths.",
        "showExportToExcel": true,
        "showAnalytics": true,
        "queryType": 1,
        "resourceType": "microsoft.resources/tenants",
        "crossComponentResources": [
          "value::tenant"
        ],
        "visualization": "table",
        "gridSettings": {
          "filter": true,
          "formatters": [
            {
              "columnMatch": "Resource",
              "formatter": 13,
              "formatOptions": {
                "linkTarget": "Resource",
                "showIcon": true
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "name": "UnifiedFindings"
    },
    {
      "type": 3,
      "content": {
        "version": "KqlItem/1.0",
        "query": "securityresources\n| where subscriptionId in~ ({Subscription:subid})\n| where type =~ 'microsoft.security/assessments'\n| extend Resource = coalesce(tostring(properties.resourceDetails.Id), tostring(properties.resourceDetails.id), tostring(properties.resourceDetails.AzureResourceId)), ResourceType = tolower(tostring(properties.resourceDetails.ResourceType)), CloudSource = tostring(properties.resourceDetails.Source), ConnectorId = tostring(properties.resourceDetails.ConnectorId)\n| extend ContextLookupId = tolower(iff(ResourceType startswith 'microsoft.hybridcompute/', Resource, ConnectorId))\n| join kind=leftouter (\n    resources\n    | where subscriptionId in~ ({Subscription:subid})\n    | where type in~ ('microsoft.hybridcompute/machines', 'microsoft.security/securityconnectors')\n    | project ContextLookupId = tolower(id), ArcCloudProvider = tostring(properties.cloudMetadata.provider), ConnectorPlatform = tostring(properties.environmentName)\n) on ContextLookupId\n| extend Environment = case(CloudSource in~ ('AzureDevOps', 'Github', 'GitLab') or ConnectorPlatform in~ ('AzureDevOps', 'Github', 'GitLab') or ResourceType contains 'devops' or ResourceType contains 'github' or ResourceType contains 'gitlab', 'DevOps', CloudSource =~ 'AWS' or ArcCloudProvider =~ 'AWS' or ConnectorPlatform =~ 'AWS' or ResourceType startswith 'microsoft.awsconnector/', 'AWS', CloudSource =~ 'GCP' or ArcCloudProvider =~ 'GCP' or ConnectorPlatform =~ 'GCP' or ResourceType startswith 'microsoft.gcpconnector/', 'GCP', CloudSource in~ ('DockerHub', 'JFrog') or ConnectorPlatform in~ ('DockerHub', 'JFrog'), 'Other', ResourceType startswith 'microsoft.hybridcompute/', 'Hybrid', CloudSource =~ 'Azure' and (isempty(ConnectorId) or ConnectorPlatform =~ 'Azure'), 'Azure', 'Other')\n| extend Workload = case(Environment == 'DevOps', 'DevOps', ResourceType has_any ('sites', 'containerapps', 'containergroups', 'lambdafunctions', 'functions'), 'Serverless', ResourceType =~ 'microsoft.containerregistry/registries' or ResourceType has_any ('containerimage', 'containerimages', 'container', 'containers', 'managedclusters', 'connectedclusters', 'eksclusters', 'kubernetesclusters'), 'Containers', ResourceType has_any ('virtualmachines', 'virtualmachinescalesets', 'machines', 'ec2instances', 'computeinstances'), 'Machines', 'Other')\n| where '{Environment}' == 'All' or Environment == '{Environment}'\n| where '{Workload}' == 'All' or Workload == '{Workload}'\n| extend Status = tostring(properties.status.code)\n| summarize ReportedRecommendations = dcount(id), Unhealthy = countif(Status == 'Unhealthy'), Healthy = countif(Status == 'Healthy'), NotApplicable = countif(Status == 'NotApplicable'), MissingStatus = countif(isempty(Status)) by Environment, Workload\n| order by Environment asc, Workload asc",
        "size": 0,
        "title": "Broader posture recommendation evidence - not Log4j verdicts",
        "noDataMessage": "No posture assessment evidence returned for this environment/workload. Verify RBAC, selected scope, onboarding, and the native Defender experience; this is not a clean result.",
        "showExportToExcel": true,
        "showAnalytics": true,
        "queryType": 1,
        "resourceType": "microsoft.resourcegraph/resources",
        "crossComponentResources": [
          "{Subscription}"
        ],
        "visualization": "table",
        "gridSettings": {
          "filter": true
        }
      },
      "name": "PostureEvidence"
    },
    {
      "type": 12,
      "content": {
        "version": "NotebookGroup/1.0",
        "groupType": "editable",
        "items": [
          {
            "type": 1,
            "content": {
              "json": "### Organization coverage - Foundational CSPM through paid protection\n| Evidence layer | What it contributes | What it does not establish |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Foundational CSPM / reported Free tier | Basic posture, inventory/recommendations, and supported connector visibility | That every Log4j dependency was scanned |\n| Paid Defender CSPM | Supported agentless machine/image scanning, risk/attack paths, SBOM and advanced DevOps context | Runtime EDR, complete unsupported-package coverage, or successful scans merely because a plan is enabled |\n| Defender for Servers / Containers / App Service and Endpoint | Applicable vulnerability assessment and workload runtime telemetry | Coverage for every resource or package without onboarding/components |\n| Connected DevOps scanners | Reported dependency/code/IaC findings and, where supported, SBOM | Dependency scanning from a connector, secret scan, or SAST alone |\n\n**Plans are context, not tabs or finding gates.** The following table starts from visible Azure subscriptions and left-joins reported plan records, so a missing pricing record remains **Unknown**, not automatically Foundational or paid. Azure anchor plans do not determine AWS/GCP/DevOps entitlements; inspect connector offerings and native coverage. Component settings, resource overrides, portal migrations, exclusions, and scan results still require verification. Nothing here enables a paid plan."
            },
            "name": "CapabilityLayers"
          },
          {
            "type": 3,
            "content": {
              "version": "KqlItem/1.0",
              "query": "resourcecontainers\n| where subscriptionId in~ ({Subscription:subid})\n| where type =~ 'microsoft.resources/subscriptions'\n| project Subscription = subscriptionId, SubscriptionName = name, SubscriptionState = tostring(properties.state)\n| join kind=leftouter (\n    securityresources\n    | where subscriptionId in~ ({Subscription:subid})\n    | where type =~ 'microsoft.security/pricings'\n    | where name in~ ('CloudPosture', 'VirtualMachines', 'Containers', 'AppServices')\n    | summarize PlanRecords = make_bag(pack(name, properties)) by Subscription = subscriptionId\n) on Subscription\n| extend ReportedCSPMTier = tostring(PlanRecords.CloudPosture.pricingTier)\n| extend CSPMEvidence = case(ReportedCSPMTier =~ 'Standard', 'Paid Defender CSPM reported', ReportedCSPMTier =~ 'Free', 'Foundational / Free reported', 'Unknown - verify native plan management')\n| project SubscriptionName, Subscription, SubscriptionState, CSPMEvidence, ReportedCSPMTier, ServersTier = tostring(PlanRecords.VirtualMachines.pricingTier), ServersSubPlan = tostring(PlanRecords.VirtualMachines.subPlan), ContainersTier = tostring(PlanRecords.Containers.pricingTier), AppServiceTier = tostring(PlanRecords.AppServices.pricingTier), PlanRecords\n| order by SubscriptionName asc",
              "size": 0,
              "title": "Visible Azure subscriptions and reported plan evidence",
              "noDataMessage": "No subscription records returned. Verify the intended tenant, selected subscriptions, and permissions; do not infer Foundational or paid coverage from missing records.",
              "showExportToExcel": true,
              "showAnalytics": true,
              "queryType": 1,
              "resourceType": "microsoft.resourcegraph/resources",
              "crossComponentResources": [
                "{Subscription}"
              ],
              "visualization": "table",
              "gridSettings": {
                "filter": true
              }
            },
            "name": "PlanCoverage"
          }
        ]
      },
      "conditionalVisibility": {
        "parameterName": "Environment",
        "comparison": "isEqualTo",
        "value": "All"
      },
      "name": "OrganizationCoverage"
    },
    {
      "type": 3,
      "content": {
        "version": "KqlItem/1.0",
        "query": "resources\n| where subscriptionId in~ ({Subscription:subid})\n| where type =~ 'microsoft.security/securityconnectors'\n| extend ConnectedPlatform = tostring(properties.environmentName), EnvironmentType = tostring(properties.environmentData.environmentType)\n| extend Environment = case(ConnectedPlatform in~ ('Github', 'AzureDevOps', 'GitLab'), 'DevOps', ConnectedPlatform =~ 'AWS', 'AWS', ConnectedPlatform =~ 'GCP', 'GCP', ConnectedPlatform =~ 'Azure', 'Azure', 'Other')\n| where '{Environment}' == 'All' or Environment == '{Environment}'\n| project Environment, ConnectedPlatform, Connector = name, EnvironmentType, ConnectedScope = tostring(properties.hierarchyIdentifier), Offerings = properties.offerings, ConnectionEvidence = 'Discovered - health and scan completion not verified', ConnectorId = id, AnchorSubscription = subscriptionId, ResourceGroup = resourceGroup\n| order by Environment asc, ConnectedPlatform asc, Connector asc",
        "size": 0,
        "title": "Discovered Defender for Cloud connectors - independent of Log4j findings",
        "noDataMessage": "No matching connector records returned. Verify scope, permissions, and onboarding. Native Azure/Arc need not have an external connector; absence of connector rows is not a clean vulnerability result.",
        "showExportToExcel": true,
        "showAnalytics": true,
        "queryType": 1,
        "resourceType": "microsoft.resourcegraph/resources",
        "crossComponentResources": [
          "{Subscription}"
        ],
        "visualization": "table",
        "gridSettings": {
          "filter": true
        }
      },
      "name": "ConnectorInventory"
    },
    {
      "type": 3,
      "content": {
        "version": "KqlItem/1.0",
        "query": "resources\n| where subscriptionId in~ ({Subscription:subid})\n| where type in~ ('microsoft.compute/virtualmachines', 'microsoft.hybridcompute/machines')\n| extend ArcCloudProvider = tostring(properties.cloudMetadata.provider)\n| extend Environment = case(type =~ 'microsoft.hybridcompute/machines' and ArcCloudProvider =~ 'AWS', 'AWS', type =~ 'microsoft.hybridcompute/machines' and ArcCloudProvider =~ 'GCP', 'GCP', type =~ 'microsoft.hybridcompute/machines', 'Hybrid', 'Azure')\n| where '{Environment}' == 'All' or Environment == '{Environment}'\n| where '{Workload}' in ('All', 'Machines')\n| extend MachineId = tolower(id), NodeResourceGroupKey = strcat(subscriptionId, '/', tolower(resourceGroup)), ArcConnectionStatus = iff(type =~ 'microsoft.hybridcompute/machines', tostring(properties.status), 'Not applicable - native Azure VM')\n| join kind=leftouter (\n    resources\n    | where subscriptionId in~ ({Subscription:subid})\n    | where type =~ 'microsoft.containerservice/managedclusters'\n    | project NodeResourceGroupKey = strcat(subscriptionId, '/', tolower(tostring(properties.nodeResourceGroup))), IsKubernetesNode = 1\n    | distinct NodeResourceGroupKey, IsKubernetesNode\n) on NodeResourceGroupKey\n| where isempty(IsKubernetesNode)\n| join kind=leftouter (\n    securityresources\n    | where subscriptionId in~ ({Subscription:subid})\n    | where type =~ 'microsoft.security/softwareinventories'\n    | project MachineId = tolower(substring(id, 0, indexof(tolower(id), '/providers/microsoft.security/softwareinventories/'))), HasSoftwareInventory = 1\n    | distinct MachineId, HasSoftwareInventory\n) on MachineId\n| extend InventoryEvidence = iff(isempty(HasSoftwareInventory), 'Missing - investigate scan coverage', 'Present - not proof of a complete Log4j scan')\n| project Environment, Machine = name, ArcCloudProvider, ArcConnectionStatus, InventoryEvidence, MachineId, Subscription = subscriptionId, ResourceGroup = resourceGroup, ResourceType = type\n| order by InventoryEvidence asc, Environment asc, Machine asc",
        "size": 0,
        "title": "Azure VM / Arc inventory evidence and connection gaps - not a complete asset census",
        "noDataMessage": "No matching Azure VM/Arc records returned. Verify environment/workload, scope, and RBAC. This check excludes AKS node groups and does not enumerate every VMSS, native AWS/GCP machine, never-onboarded asset, or container.",
        "showExportToExcel": true,
        "showAnalytics": true,
        "queryType": 1,
        "resourceType": "microsoft.resourcegraph/resources",
        "crossComponentResources": [
          "{Subscription}"
        ],
        "visualization": "table",
        "gridSettings": {
          "filter": true,
          "formatters": [
            {
              "columnMatch": "MachineId",
              "formatter": 13,
              "formatOptions": {
                "linkTarget": "Resource",
                "showIcon": true
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "name": "MachineInventoryCoverage"
    },
    {
      "type": 12,
      "content": {
        "version": "NotebookGroup/1.0",
        "groupType": "editable",
        "items": [
          {
            "type": 1,
            "content": {
              "json": "### Coverage and investigation notes\n- **Current data model:** individual `SoftwareUpdate` / `ServiceUpgrade` assessments replaced grouped vulnerability recommendations. Detailed CVE metadata comes from tenant-scoped `microsoft.security/cvedetails`; the assessment side is subscription-filtered. Left joins preserve findings without metadata. Missing CVE/risk context is explicitly unknown, not low risk or zero attack paths.\n- **Scanner provenance:** MDVM is the current integrated machine/image scanner. Defender CSPM contributes supported agentless scanning plus risk context, not an independent extra scanner. Agent-based and agentless results are not added together. Retired integrated Qualys and supported Qualys/Rapid7 BYOL are different offerings; no provider tab is needed.\n- **Machine coverage:** Servers P1/P2 supports the endpoint-based path; Defender CSPM or Servers P2 supports eligible agentless cloud scanning. Agentless scans are periodic, not EDR. Log4j JAR/uber-JAR coverage varies by OS, sensor, packaging, and scanning method.\n- **Container coverage:** Registry access plus supported discovery/sensor settings is required. Registry language-package scanning is Linux-only; do not promise Java coverage for Windows images. Runtime image assessment does not inspect every writable-layer change. Check scan/rescan windows and running digests.\n- **Serverless:** Serverless protection and Serverless Containers are separately enabled CSPM components with eligibility/billing limits. Current documentation places serverless VA in the Defender portal. Stopped apps, apps with public network access disabled, and documented app kinds aren't eligible for that VA. Do not broaden network access merely to obtain a scan. Serverless Containers is posture-only, not runtime EDR or active response.\n- **DevOps:** Agentless code scanning (Preview) and SBOM need supported connectors/scanners. Java dependency analysis is not Java SAST. Use native SBOM/package queries and code-to-runtime mapping; ARG findings are not SBOM inventory.\n- **Runtime:** Endpoint/XDR and workload alerts investigate suspicious activity; CSPM posture alone does not provide EDR. WAF and Firewall Premium IDPS inspect covered traffic, not every JAR. Verify managed rules, effective paranoia level, prevention mode, exclusions, TLS/inspection visibility, routing, and diagnostic ingestion.\n- **Scope and unknowns:** organization means visible data in the intended tenant/selected subscriptions. AWS/GCP provenance takes precedence over Arc representation; missing provenance remains Other. Azure anchor subscriptions are not the external environment's licensing verdict. Query limits, unsupported or never-onboarded assets, and missing metadata can leave gaps.\n\n[Machine scan coverage](https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/defender-for-cloud/enable-agentless-scanning-vms) | [Container assessment](https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/defender-for-cloud/agentless-vulnerability-assessment-azure) | [Serverless protection](https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/defender-for-cloud/serverless-protection) | [Serverless containers](https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/defender-for-cloud/posture-for-serverless-containers) | [Security explorer / attack paths](https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/defender-for-cloud/concept-attack-path)\n\n### Optional runtime alert investigation\nSelect a workspace to query `SecurityAlert`. This is **workspace/time scoped**, not narrowed by the environment, workload, subscription, or Log4j finding filters. Keyword matches are triage candidates, not a complete exploitation detector or proof of compromise. A missing table/permission produces a visible error, not a synthetic zero. Defender hunting tables such as `DeviceTvmSoftwareVulnerabilities` are not automatically available in Log Analytics.\n\n[Defender hunting guidance](https://learn.microsoft.com/defender-vulnerability-management/tvm-manage-log4shell-guidance#use-advanced-hunting) | [Front Door rules](https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/web-application-firewall/afds/waf-front-door-drs) | [Firewall Premium IDPS](https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/firewall/premium-features#idps)"
            },
            "name": "CoverageAndRuntimeGuidance"
          },
          {
            "type": 9,
            "content": {
              "version": "KqlParameterItem/1.0",
              "parameters": [
                {
                  "id": "4b56f6c1-3f9e-4e15-8d66-55caf051b003",
                  "version": "KqlParameterItem/1.0",
                  "name": "Workspace",
                  "type": 5,
                  "description": "Optional: one workspace with SecurityAlert data. This query is workspace/time scoped, not narrowed by environment, workload, subscription, or Log4j finding filters.",
                  "isRequired": false,
                  "multiSelect": false,
                  "query": "resources\n| where subscriptionId in~ ({Subscription:subid})\n| where type =~ 'microsoft.operationalinsights/workspaces'\n| project value = id, label = name",
                  "queryType": 1,
                  "resourceType": "microsoft.resourcegraph/resources",
                  "crossComponentResources": [
                    "{Subscription}"
                  ],
                  "typeSettings": {
                    "showDefault": false
                  },
                  "value": ""
                },
                {
                  "id": "4b56f6c1-3f9e-4e15-8d66-55caf051b004",
                  "version": "KqlParameterItem/1.0",
                  "name": "TimeRange",
                  "type": 4,
                  "description": "Time range for the optional workspace alert query only; ARG assessments are current state.",
                  "isRequired": true,
                  "typeSettings": {
                    "selectableValues": [
                      {
                        "durationMs": 86400000
                      },
                      {
                        "durationMs": 604800000
                      },
                      {
                        "durationMs": 2592000000
                      }
                    ],
                    "allowCustom": true
                  },
                  "value": {
                    "durationMs": 604800000
                  }
                }
              ],
              "style": "pills"
            },
            "name": "RuntimeParameters"
          },
          {
            "type": 3,
            "content": {
              "version": "KqlItem/1.0",
              "query": "SecurityAlert\n| where TimeGenerated {TimeRange}\n| where AlertName contains 'log4j' or AlertName contains 'log4shell' or Description contains 'log4j' or Description contains 'log4shell' or ExtendedProperties contains 'CVE-2021-44228' or ExtendedProperties contains 'CVE-2021-45046' or ExtendedProperties contains 'CVE-2021-45105' or ExtendedProperties contains 'CVE-2021-44832'\n| project TimeGenerated, AlertSeverity, AlertName, ProductName, CompromisedEntity, Description, SystemAlertId, AlertLink\n| order by TimeGenerated desc",
              "size": 0,
              "title": "Candidate Log4j-related alerts - selected workspace/time only",
              "noDataMessage": "No matching alerts in this workspace/time range. Verify ingestion, permissions, retention, and detection coverage. No alerts do not establish that exploitation did not occur.",
              "showExportToExcel": true,
              "showAnalytics": true,
              "queryType": 0,
              "resourceType": "microsoft.operationalinsights/workspaces",
              "crossComponentResources": [
                "{Workspace}"
              ],
              "timeContextFromParameter": "TimeRange",
              "visualization": "table",
              "gridSettings": {
                "filter": true
              }
            },
            "conditionalVisibility": {
              "parameterName": "Workspace",
              "comparison": "isNotEqualTo",
              "value": ""
            },
            "name": "RuntimeAlerts"
          }
        ]
      },
      "conditionalVisibility": {
        "parameterName": "ShowHelp",
        "comparison": "isEqualTo",
        "value": "On"
      },
      "name": "GuidanceAndInvestigation"
    }
  ],
  "fallbackResourceIds": [],
  "$schema": "https://github.com/Microsoft/Application-Insights-Workbooks/blob/master/schema/workbook.json"
}
